<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρμ-ιγξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιγγος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lyre,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, esp. as the instrument of Apollo, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρμιγγος περικαλλέος ἣν ἔχ᾽
					Ἀπόλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.603
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				24.63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.270
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				203
			</span></i>; of Achilles, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένα τερπόμενον φόρμιγγι λιγείῃ καλῇ
					δαιδαλέῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.186
				</span></i>
			; with seven strings (after Terpander's time), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑπτάκτυπος, ἑπτάγλωσσος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				5.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιψάλλων ἐλεφαντόδετον φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					219
				</span></i>
			 (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἄχορδος,</span> metaph. for a
			<i>bow,</i> Arist.<i><span class="en">
				Rh.
				1413a1
			</span></i>.</div>
